Question: Given an array of integers nums and an integer target, return indices of the two numbers such that they add up to target.

You may assume that each input would have exactly one solution, and you may not use the same element twice.

You can return the answer in any order.



Code:
class Solution {
public:
    // Function to find two indices of numbers in the array that add up to the target
    vector<int> twoSum(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int n = nums.size(); // Get the size of the input vector 'nums'
        
        // Loop through each element in the array
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            // For each element, loop through the subsequent elements
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                // Check if the sum of the two elements equals the target
                if (nums[i] + nums[j] == target) {
                    // If found, return the indices of the two elements
                    return {i, j};
                }
            }
        }
        // If no two elements sum up to the target, return an empty vector
        return {}; 
    }
};
